      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Latitudes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are parallel lines running east-west that measure angular distance north or south of the Equator.",
        "Longitudes are vertical lines connecting the North and South Poles, measured east or west from the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is calculated from the 82.5° E meridian passing through Mirzapur, Uttar Pradesh.",
        "The Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N) passes through eight Indian states from west to east.",
        "The Equator (0°) crosses three continents: South America, Africa, and Asia."
      ],
      "id": "joj9qtr"
